  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 73ff519377b990a4c81cd1461a3c1f62, type: 3}
  m_Name: Kalaw_Intro
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueNode
  speakerName: Kalaw
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: e9a1f2822809deb49a0ce098da0fddca, type: 3}
  dialogueText: "Squawk! Look at you, traveler!\nYou've walked the streets of Vigan,
    shared moments with the people of Ilocos, and learned the words and expressions
    that bring our everyday conversations to life.\nBut remember this: learning a
    language is more than simply repeating words after someone else. A language is
    a bridge\u2014a way to understand people, share stories, and become part of a
    community.\nTo truly learn a language, you must listen and understand, choose
    the right words, create your own sentences, and find the courage to speak\u2014even
    when the situation changes and the words don't come easily.\nEvery word you learn
    brings you one step closer to the people who speak it. Every sentence you form
    gives your voice a little more strength.\nSo don't be afraid to make mistakes,
    traveler. Keep listening. Keep speaking. Keep learning.\nBecause when you learn
    a language, you don't just learn how to speak. You learn how to connect."
  translatedText: 
